but engineers here have figured out how to get them to make hurricane strength winds. And that's why I'm here, because this is a lab where researchers are figuring out how we can make our homes and infrastructure survive hurricanes better, especially at a time when more intense storms are going to be more frequent. What shape should a roof be so it stands a better chance of not getting blown off? Is it possible to make stronger doors?
但这里的工程师们已经摸索出如何让它们产生飓风强度的风。这就是我来这里的原因，因为这是一个实验室，研究人员正在这里寻找如何让我们的房屋和基础设施更好地抵御飓风的方法，尤其是在更强烈的风暴将更加频繁出现的时代。屋顶应该是什么形状，才能有更大几率不被风吹掀？有可能制造出更坚固的门吗？

