Changed research. Changed the building codes. All of those things were accelerated after Hurricane Andrew. Meteorologists designated Hurricane Andrew a so-called category 5 storm. Even if you don't know much about hurricanes, you know a category 5 is major. It's actually the highest classification according to the scale we use to measure these
改变了研究。改变了建筑法规。所有这些都在安德鲁飓风之后加速推进了。气象学家将安德鲁飓风指定为所谓的 5 级风暴。即使你对飓风了解不多，你也知道 5 级是一场重大灾难。事实上，根据我们用来衡量这些事情的尺度，这是最高的分类。

10
00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:41.000
things. The Saffir-Simpson Hurricane Wind Scale. For 50 years, the Saffir-Simpson Scale has been used to talk about how to build more resilient communities. It's been the language that we all rely on to understand what kind of risk a hurricane poses. During storm emergencies, we are primed to hear about categories. And the scale has transcended hurricanes.
萨菲尔-辛普森飓风风力等级。50 年来，萨菲尔-辛普森等级一直被用于探讨如何建设更具韧性的社区。它一直是我们赖以理解飓风构成何种风险的语言。在风暴紧急情况下，我们已经习惯了听闻各种级别。而这个等级已经超越了飓风本身。

11
00:04:41.000 --> 00:05:21.000
It's been adopted as a common shorthand for describing damage of all kinds. We use it for situations that have absolutely nothing to do with weather. — Midterm madness, more like a category four hurricane. — We're now treating this like a massive cat five hurricane disaster. — Homeland Security Secretary Nielsen there, sounding the alarm on the immigration crisis ahead of— — Donald Trump is a cat five disaster for American political discourse. The reason the Saffir-Simpson scale has been adapted so much is because it's really good at what it does. It's a clear, easy shorthand for damage.
它已被采纳为描述各种伤害的通用简写。我们将其用于与天气完全无关的情况。——期中疯狂，更像是一场 4 级飓风。——我们现在正将此视同为一场大规模的 5 级飓风灾难。——国土安全部长尼尔森在那里就即将到来的移民危机拉响警报————唐纳德·特朗普对美国政治话语体系来说是一场 5 级灾难。萨菲尔-辛普森等级之所以被如此广泛地调整使用，是因为它在所做的事情上非常出色。它是一种关于损失的清晰、简单的简写。

12
00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:53.000
It tells us what we can expect from different categories of hurricane strength winds, what they're likely to do to our homes, to our infrastructure, and our communities. It's a snapshot of probable impact. The thing is, five decades on, we've got different homes, different infrastructure, different communities. Scientists say even our hurricanes are different these days. And there are doubts now about whether the Saffir-Simpson scale is telling us enough in that snapshot and whether it still serves this changing world we live in.
它告诉我们，我们可以从不同级别的飓风强度风力中预期什么，它们可能会对我们的家园、基础设施和社区造成什么影响。它是可能造成影响的快照。问题是，五十年过去了，我们有了不同的家园、不同的基础设施、不同的社区。科学家们表示，如今连我们的飓风都变了。现在人们开始怀疑，萨菲尔-辛普森等级在那个快照中是否向我们提供足够的信息，以及它是否仍然服务于我们生活的这个不断变化的世界。

