00:05:53.000 --> 00:06:21.000
Because hurricanes are so chaotic, they've always been a bit tricky to characterize, even in an age of satellites and radar. They're capricious. They can get stronger or weaker and change direction quickly. No two are the same. And even a single hurricane isn't uniform all the way around. They have a stronger side and a weaker one. You know, hurricanes are facts of nature. The best that we can do is forecast them,
因为飓风具有极大的混乱性，它们一直有点难以描述，即使在卫星和雷达时代也是如此。它们变化无常。它们可能会变强或变弱，并迅速改变方向。没有哪两个飓风是相同的。甚至单一飓风在四周也不是均匀的。它们有一侧更强，另一侧更弱。你知道，飓风是大自然的客观事实。我们能做的最好的事情就是预测它们、

