and promoted their own West Indian hurricane warning systems instead. And a lot of that, as I described in the book, really had to do with the condescending attitude that the American meteorologists had towards their fellow meteorologists. And that was much the detriment of the Americans. They paid the price almost immediately.
转而推广他们自己的西印度群岛飓风预警系统。正如我在书中所描述的那样，这在很大程度上与美国气象学家对其他气象学家抱有的那种居高临下的态度有关。这极大地损害了美国人自身的利益。他们几乎立刻就付出了代价。

