00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:50.000
In September of 1900, Cuban meteorologists warned of a storm that was going to intensify, turn into a hurricane, and head to the Gulf of Mexico. And the Americans were not paying attention to the valuable meteorological information that the Cubans were providing providing and they missed some of the signs and information that the Cubans had been tracking. They knew that it was a hurricane. It wasn't until the very last moment that the American meteorologists finally said, oh this is a hurricane. By then it was almost too late. Galveston's population was 38,000 people at the time, and as many as 8,000 people died.
1900 年 9 月，古巴气象学家发出警告，称一场风暴将会加剧、变成飓风，并直奔墨西哥湾。而美国人却没有重视古巴人提供的宝贵气象信息，他们漏掉了古巴人一直在追踪的一些迹象和信息。他们知道这是一场飓风。直到最后一刻，美国气象学家才终于说，哦，这是一场飓风。到那时已经几乎太迟了。加尔维斯顿当时的人口为 38,000 人，多达 8,000 人丧生。

