00:10:50.000 --> 00:11:20.000
It's one thing to know generally that a storm is coming. It's another to forecast that it's going to be a deadly calamity. And it would be decades before the U.S. began making real progress in understanding hurricanes. That big leap came from a pair of cocky World War II pilots. The two airmen, also in Galveston, as it happens, made a bet to show how tough their planes were. And this was taking a plane, deliberately flying it into a hurricane, through the wall of a hurricane, into the eye of the hurricane.
笼统地知道风暴即将来临是一回事。预测它将是一场致命的灾难则是另一回事。美国需要几十年时间才能在理解飓风方面取得实质性进展。那个巨大的飞跃来自两名趾高气扬的二战飞行员。这两名飞行员碰巧也在加尔维斯顿，他们打了个赌，以展示他们的飞机有多坚固。他们驾驶一架飞机，蓄意飞进飓风中，穿过飓风壁，进入飓风眼。

