00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:51.000
But we still didn't have a way to communicate that forecast clearly and concisely, or a way to show the public what warnings were actually based on to prove that they were worth heeding. That step was taken by the most trusted voice in broadcasting at the time, Edward R. Murrow. — In mid-September of 1954, he decided to hop into a Hurricane Hunter plane and go and fly into the center of what was called Hurricane Edna, which was threatening the East Coast. Good evening.
