00:27:04.000 --> 00:28:00.000
and maybe expanding it to include a category six. You look at the science and the science says, higher number of more intense storms. Okay, well, let's think about that in terms of a scale that was developed 50 years ago. It's time to have that debate. He remembers watching Dorian's path in 2019, when it looked like that hurricane would hit South Florida. It was going to be like Andrew all over again, only worse. That brought it home. It was like a lightning bolt right between my eyes. And I said, okay, I don't know how to describe to the media what it feels like to be looking at sustained winds of 185 miles an hour, less than 30 hours from my house.
并可能将其扩大到包括 6 级的人之一。你看看科学，科学表明，更强烈的风暴数量会更多。好吧，让我们结合 50 年前制定的等级来思考这个问题。是时候展开这场辩论了。他记得在 2019 年观看多利安的路径时，当时看起来那场飓风将袭击南佛罗里达。那将是又一次安德鲁风暴重演，甚至更糟。这让他感同身受。这就像一道闪电直击我的双眼。我说，好吧，我不知道该如何向媒体形容，直面距离我家不到 30 小时、持续风速达到每小时 185 英里的风暴是什么感觉。

54
00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:26.000
Climate change has forced scientists to make other adjustments to their extreme weather warning systems. The Australian Bureau of Meteorology added two new colors, pink and purple, to their maps to convey record-breaking heat. So maybe a six would expand our vocabulary for this greater risk and drive home the urgency of climate change. And the Saffir-Simpson Hurricane Scale is from 1974. Maybe it could use an update.
气候变化迫使科学家对其极端天气预警系统做出其他调整。澳大利亚气象局在地图上添加了两种新颜色——粉色和紫色——来传达破纪录的高温。所以也许一个 6 级会扩大我们应对这种更大风险的词汇量，并坚定传达气候变化的紧迫性。而萨菲尔-辛普森飓风等级自 1974 年起就存在了。或许它确实需要更新。

55
00:28:26.000 --> 00:28:51.000
It describes damage as though all structures are created equal. But of course that isn't true. Some areas have more vulnerable infrastructure than others. You could have a Category 2 storm that gives you the long-term power outages of a Category 5. Besides, a lot has changed about how we build stuff. Maybe Bob Simpson's reasoning that it's all the same damage after five just isn't true anymore.
它对破坏的描述就好像所有建筑生而平等一样。但事实当然并非如此。有些地区的基础设施比其他地区更脆弱。你可能会遭遇一场 2 级风暴，却带来 5 级风暴那样的长期停电。此外，我们建造东西的方式已经发生了很大变化。也许鲍勃·辛普森关于“过 5 级之后破坏都一样”的推论现在已经不再成立了。

