It's not the same built environment as it was 30, 40 years ago. Fifty even. I can't believe that that's absolutely true. Yes, now I feel really old. Okay. It just says to me that we need to have the academic government open kind of debate. But the National Hurricane Center, which administers the scale and is in charge of categorizing hurricanes, isn't keen on adding a six to Saffir-Simpson. There's a fear in the scientific community that expanding it would do more harm than good.
这里的建筑环境已经与 30、40 年前不同了。甚至 50 年前。我无法相信那是绝对正确的。好吧，现在我真的觉得自己老了。好吧。这对我来说只是意味着我们需要开展学术界与政府公开形式的辩论。但负责管理该等级并负责飓风分类的国家飓风中心并不热衷于在萨菲尔-辛普森中增加 6 级。科学界有一种担忧，即扩大它会弊大于利。

57
