when it gets to be three, four, five, but we have really started to shy away from using it for everything. Robbie Berg with the NHC says it was a big problem during Hurricane Florence in 2018. Florence had gotten strong. It got to a major hurricane strength. It was reaching or heading toward North Carolina and it began to weaken a little bit as it was approaching the coast. It weakened so much that it was no longer technically a hurricane. But the hazards with the storm, the rainfall we were expecting, the storm surge we
当风暴达到三级、四级、五级时，但我们确实已经开始回避在所有事情上都使用它。国家飓风中心的罗比·伯格（Robbie Berg）表示，这在2018年的飓风“佛罗伦萨”期间是一个大问题。佛罗伦萨当时变得很强。它达到了大型飓风的强度。它当时正在接近或朝着北卡罗来纳州移动，在接近海岸时开始稍微减弱。它减弱得如此厉害，以至于在技术上不再是飓风。但是风暴带来的灾难、我们预期的降雨、我们预期的风暴潮

